From c0f7aaf26b74810645ba021d9cd04fbef88ba2a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:08:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 39/40] Recover the reference delayed-ACK policy

tcp_delay_ack moves the delay decision from the congestion-control
modules into tcp_ack.c as an external _Bool helper.  Modes 1 and 2
delay only when no zero window was advertised, the peer did not set
TH_PUSH, and exactly one segment is unacknowledged.  Mode 3 computes
the announceable receive window (clamped by the negotiated scale) and
delays when the socket has data above sb_lowat, the window is not
growing, the gap since the last ACK is within an MSS or the window is
more than 1.5 * tcp_recvspace, the gap is under a quarter window and
256 segments; it counts the delay in t_stat.acks_delayed.

The reference tables leave every tcp_cc_algo.delay_ack slot NULL, so
remove tcp_cc_delay_ack and the four per-algorithm wrappers, and have
the tcp_input DELAY_ACK macro call tcp_delay_ack directly.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
